==============================================================================
FC-AeST kernel bridge (f_G=1/2)
==============================================================================
  [ok] x = g_phi/a0 = (y/2)(1+e^-y)   [derived: y/2 + y*exp(-y)/2]
  [ok] mu~(x) = f_G mu_obs/(1-f_G mu_obs) = tanh(y/2)   [tanh(y/2)]
  [ok] dx/dy = (1/2)[1+(1-y)e^-y]   [(-y + exp(y) + 1)*exp(-y)/2]
  [ok] dx/dy > 0 for all y>=0 (min at y=2 = (1-e^-2)/2 = 0.432) => x<->y invertible

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Asymptotic limits survive the translation:
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  [ok] deep-MOND: mu_obs ~ y => g_N=g^2/a0 => g=sqrt(a0 g_N) => v^4=G a0 M (BTFR)
  [ok] Newtonian: mu_obs->1 => g_N->g (g_phi->g_N/2, g=g_phi+g_N/2->g_N)
  [ok] field mu~: ->1 Newtonian, ~ y/2 deep-MOND (healthy interpolation, mu~ in (0,1))
  J'_FC(x^2) = mu~(x) = tanh(y(x)/2);  J_FC(x^2) = INT_0^{x^2} tanh(y(sqrt u)/2) du  (AeST F-sector)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Cosmological lock (the FC novelty):
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  a0^2(Q) = -kappa^2 c^2 G K(Q),  K(Q)=-(1/2)F(0,Q)  =>  a0(z)=kappa c sqrt(G rho_DE(z))
  with rho_DE(z) := -K[Qbar(z)]  =>  a0(z)/a0,0 = sqrt(rho_DE(z)/rho_DE,0)  =>  a0 PROPORTIONAL sqrt(rho_DE)
  LIMIT w=-1 (Lambda): rho_DE=const => a0=const (flat, matches STANDING 'nearly flat in MOND regime').
  This SUPERSEDES the naive a0(z) proportional H(z) (STANDING: H(z) reading disfavoured ~2.3 sigma).
  Distinctive ONLY if DE evolves -- exactly what DESI DR2/DR3 probe (evolving-DE preference ~few sigma).

